# WASM PV1 — Hostile IDENT if is not a const-true fold

File: openOODA/audit/wasm_pv1.oot
PV1 red team. WASM lane. Source proof only. Did not edit fixtures or smokes.
C emit + gcc stays the everyday path. Did not rebuild.

Logline: The hostile if condition is IDENT x, not KW_TRUE or KW_FALSE, and the smoke fails only on a fold-me-only print or plant.
Setup: Read `ooda/fixtures/wasm_if_hostile.oo`, `ooda/scripts/wasm_if_hostile_smoke.oo`, `ooda/oodac/token_emit.oo`, and `ooda/oodac/wasm_emit_if.oo`. Drive words are source. Did not exec emit-wasm.
Beats:
  1. Quote the hostile main body.
  2. Prove the if condition token is IDENT x.
  3. Prove the product fail is only fold-me-only stdout or bytes.

## 0. Verdict

PASS

The fixture is a non-const if. The condition is IDENT `x`.
It is not KW_TRUE. It is not KW_FALSE.
The named smoke fails the product path only when `fold-me` is
present and `other` is absent.

Dummy empty stdout, ERR, wasmtime fail, no `fold-me`, and both
strings present all pass. That is the hostile lock.

## 1. Hostile shape quote

File: `ooda/fixtures/wasm_if_hostile.oo` (19 lines).

Header Setup: "Condition is IDENT x, not KW_TRUE."
Header Beat 3: "A fold-me-only module is a lie."

Main body, exact:

    pub fn main() {
        let x = true;
        if x {
            println("fold-me");
        } else {
            println("other");
        }
    }

COORD bar (`audit/wasm_coord.oot` lock 3) names this same shape.

Contrast (not this fixture):

  `fixtures/wasm_if_true.oo`  — `if true { println("then-yes"); ... }`
  `fixtures/wasm_if_false.oo` — `if false { println("then-no"); ... }`

Those two use the true and false keywords. This one does not.

## 2. Condition is IDENT x

Token row is four tab fields: kind, line, col, text.
`field_at(..., 0)` is kind. `field_at(..., 3)` is text.

`token_emit.oo` `keyword_kind`:

    if id == "true" { return "KW_TRUE"; }
    if id == "false" { return "KW_FALSE"; }
    return "IDENT";

`x` is not `true`. `x` is not `false`. Kind is IDENT. Text is `x`.

The let initializer `true` is KW_TRUE. That is not the if slot.
A fold that copies the let into the if would treat IDENT `x` as
const-true and plant `fold-me` only. That is the lie.

`wasm_fn_if_println` (`wasm_emit_if.oo`) after the fname LBRACE:

  1. Next kind must be KW_IF. Else return "".
  2. Next kind `ck` must be KW_TRUE or KW_FALSE. Else return "".
  3. IDENT returns "". INT returns "".

Hostile after main LBRACE is KW_LET, not KW_IF. First miss.
Hostile if slot is IDENT `x`, not KW_TRUE or KW_FALSE. Second miss.

The helper never walks a let. It never treats IDENT as const-true.

Other emit helpers also miss this body:

  ident-let wants `let IDENT = STRING; println(IDENT);`
    Hostile let value is KW_TRUE, not STRING. Next stmt is KW_IF.
  print-lit, strcat, two-println, int-lit want println first.
  hello fold wants `let IDENT = greet(STRING);`.

So emit must keep dummy `end` or write ERR. It must not plant
`fold-me` alone.

## 3. Smoke fails only on fold-me-only

File: `ooda/scripts/wasm_if_hostile_smoke.oo` (76 lines).
Drive: `./oodac/oodac emit-wasm fixtures/wasm_if_hostile.oo`.

`fail(msg)` is the only exit-1 path. Call sites:

  harness: `mkdir`, `scenario`, `no oodac`, `no fixture`
  product: `fail("fold-me-only")` only, in `refuse_fold_me_only`

No `fail` on missing magic. No `fail` on dummy `02 00 0b`.
No `fail` on empty stdout. No `fail` on wasmtime crash.
No `fail` when `other` is also present.

Honest PASS, then return:

  1. emit-wasm process_exec is Err and stderr has `ERR`.
  2. `^ERR` on stderr or on the wasm path.
  3. wasmtime is present and `check` is Err (run fail).
  4. Else fall through to `refuse_fold_me_only`, then print PASSED.

`refuse_fold_me_only(p, path, bytes)`:

  stdout path (`bytes == false`): empty file returns. Honest.
  `gfold` is `grep -q fold-me` (or `grep -a` on bytes).
  `goth` is `grep -q other` (or `grep -a` on bytes).
  `fail("fold-me-only")` runs only when `gfold` is ok and `goth`
  is err. That is: `fold-me` present, `other` absent.

Product matrix:

  | stdout or bytes | smoke |
  | --- | --- |
  | ERR / emit fail with ERR | PASS |
  | empty stdout | PASS |
  | dummy bytes, no `fold-me` | PASS |
  | wasmtime fail | PASS |
  | no `fold-me` (other may be present) | PASS |
  | `fold-me` and `other` | PASS |
  | `fold-me` without `other` | FAIL `fold-me-only` |

When wasmtime is present and the run exits 0, the check is stdout.
When wasmtime is absent, the check is wasm bytes (`grep -a`).

A const-true IDENT fold prints or plants `fold-me` and drops
`other`. That is the only product fail.

Bound: if wasmtime is present and the run is Err, the smoke
passes and does not scan bytes. That is still not a fail on
dummy or ERR. The product fail string stays `fold-me-only`.

